%I A401354 #10 Oct 31 2026 20:20:51
%S A401354 1,1,3,12,62,446,7503,1258518,3672523869
%N A401354 Number of nonisomorphic abelian doppelsemigroups of order n.
%C A401354 Also, a(n) is the number of nonisomorphic semigroups of order n that are both right-commutative and left-commutative.
%C A401354 A doppelsemigroup is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A401354    (x -| y) |- z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A401354    (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z).
%C A401354 A doppelsemigroup (D,-|,|-) is called abelian if x -| y = y |- x for all x,y from D.
%C A401354 A semigroup S is called right-commutative (left-commutative) if axy = ayx (xya = yxa) for all a,x,y from S.
%H A401354 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23395740">Enumeration and lists of nonisomorphic semigroups that are both right-commutative and left-commutative</a>, Zenodo (2026).
%H A401354 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/1f9618f849e5421579639f43070dd5da">C++ program for computing all pairwise nonisomorphic semigroups that are both right-commutative and left-commutative</a>, GitHub Gist (2026).
%H A401354 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.15421/242602">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, Res. Math., 34(1) (2026), 16-33.
%H A401354 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.28908">Note on the number of doppelsemigroups of small order</a>, arXiv:2606.28908 [math.GR], (2026).
%H A401354 Anatolii V. Zhuchok and Kolja Knauer, <a href="https://admjournal.luguniv.edu.ua/index.php/adm/article/view/1249/pdf">Abelian doppelsemigroups</a>, Algebra Discrete Math., 26(2) (2018), 290-304.
%e A401354 For n = 2, there are exactly 3 nonisomorphic abelian doppelsemigroups (D,-|,|-) on the set D = {0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all three doppelsemigroups are listed below.
%e A401354 Doppelsemigroup #1:
%e A401354   -|:   |-:
%e A401354   0 0   0 0
%e A401354   0 0   0 0
%e A401354 Doppelsemigroup #2:
%e A401354   -|:   |-:
%e A401354   0 0   0 0
%e A401354   0 1   0 1
%e A401354 Doppelsemigroup #3:
%e A401354   -|:   |-:
%e A401354   0 1   0 1
%e A401354   1 0   1 0
%Y A401354 Cf. A399676, A399678, A399679, A401298, A027851, A001426, A383885.
